"""
emerge -- a Portage-flavoured front-end for Debian systems.

One file, two backends, zero dependencies beyond the Python stdlib:

  apt backend   used automatically when apt-get is present. Thin wrapper:
                apt resolves, downloads, verifies and installs; this script
                translates the experience into emerge. depclean delegates
                to `apt-get autoremove` (apt's auto/manual marks are the
                source of truth).

  dpkg backend  used automatically when apt-get is absent (embedded boxes
                with dpkg only). Implements the repository layer itself:
                parses /etc/apt/sources.list and deb822 .sources files
                (create one by hand on apt-less systems), syncs Packages
                indexes over http(s):// or file://, resolves dependencies
                natively (Depends, Pre-Depends, or-deps, Provides,
                Conflicts/Breaks), verifies SHA256, drives dpkg directly,
                and keeps a real world file for Portage-style --depclean.
                A file:// flat source pointing at a bare directory of
                .deb files (USB stick) works too: --sync generates the
                missing Packages index with dpkg-deb.

Force a backend with --backend=apt|dpkg or EMERGE_BACKEND=dpkg.

Sets behave like Portage's: @world = @selected + @system, where
@selected is the world file (dpkg backend) or apt's manual-install marks
(apt backend), and @system is Debian's Essential/Priority:required base.
Sets expand into targets, so they mix freely with atoms and each other.

Atoms are Debian package names. A Portage category is accepted and ignored
(app-misc/sl means sl), since Debian has none. For an exact version use
apt's spelling, sl=5.02-1+b1, rather than Portage's =sl-5.02-1+b1; version
ranges have no command-line equivalent, and --no-dep-upgrade is what holds
installed versions down. A path to a .deb is passed to apt as it stands.

Flags compose like Gentoo's:

    emerge cowsay              # installed and current? re-merge (reinstall)
    emerge -u cowsay           # update only if outdated; install if missing
    emerge -u @world           # update packages in the world set only
    emerge -uD @world          # --deep: update the whole dependency tree
    emerge @system -pv         # re-merge the base system (try with -p first!)
    emerge --sync
    emerge -s python           # -S searches descriptions too
    emerge -C cowsay
    emerge --depclean [-p]
    emerge -f vim              # fetchonly
    emerge -1 strace           # oneshot: don't record in world (dpkg backend)

Paths (dpkg backend): tree /var/lib/emerge-dpkg/tree, world file
/var/lib/emerge-dpkg/world, distfiles /var/cache/emerge-dpkg/distfiles.
"""

